history. The Edge Function injects a specialized system prompt ('You are CodeMeet+ 
Assistant, a helpful AI like ChatGPT...') and proxies the request to the Google Gemini 3 
Flash / OpenAI model gateway. By returning a `text/event-stream` body, tokens are 
parsed in real time and appended to the UI buffer: 
const reader = resp.body.getReader(); 
const decoder = new TextDecoder(); 
while (true) { 
  const { done, value } = await reader.read(); 
  if (done) break; 
  buf += decoder.decode(value, { stream: true }); 
  // Process SSE lines data: {...} 
  const p = JSON.parse(line.slice(6)); 
  acc += p.choices?.[0]?.delta?.content || ''; 
  setMessages((m) => m.map((x, i) => i === m.length - 1 ? { ...x, content: acc } : 
x)); 
} 
5.4.6  In-Meeting Chat & Persistent Direct Messaging 
CodeMeet+ incorporates two distinct messaging tiers: synchronous in-meeting chat 
(supporting both room-wide broadcasts and private peer messages stored in 
`meeting_messages`) and asynchronous direct messaging (`Chat.tsx`). The DM module 
includes contact search, conversation history, and secure binary file attachments uploaded 
directly to the Supabase Storage bucket `chat-files`. The following handler illustrates file 
serialization and persistent message dispatch: 
const handleSendDM = async (text: string, file?: File) => { 
  let fileUrl: string | null = null; 
  if (file) { 
    const fileExt = file.name.split('.').pop(); 
    const filePath = `${user.id}/${Date.now()}.${fileExt}`; 
    const { error: upErr } = await supabase.storage.from('chat-
files').upload(filePath, file); 
    if (!upErr) { 
      const { data: pubData } = supabase.storage.from('chat-
files').getPublicUrl(filePath); 
      fileUrl = pubData.publicUrl; 
    } 
  } 
  await supabase.from('direct_messages').insert({ 
    sender_id: user.id, 
    recipient_id: activePeerId, 
    content: text, 
    file_url: fileUrl, 
    file_name: file?.name || null 
  }); 
};
